Hi Hardin,

Sorry, that's a problem I have been meaning to fix for a long time. Fortunately, there is a simple (but not obvious) fix. You need to add all the levels to your factor in newdata, even if it only contains one of those levels. Try this:

> nd2 <- data.frame(hab=factor("Hammock", levels=c("Hammock","Marsh","Pineland","Swamp")), roadDist=seq(min(AnoleSites$roadDist),max(AnoleSites$roadDist),length=100))

> predict(asa5, newdata = nd2, type = "state")

Note that nd2$hab only has the value "Hammock", but it is now associated with the other 4 levels. Please let us know if this works... or doesn't.

Richard

